        {
          "id": "meaning",
          "title": "Meaning",
          "type": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Represents Keon (Heaven and Light), symbolizing the origin of all things in the universe, the genesis of creation, and the pure beginning of the martial journey."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "philosophy",
          "title": "Philosophy",
          "type": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "Perform with upright grandeur, clear cadence, and steady forward vision like the morning sun ascending into a clear sky."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "trigram",
          "title": "Trigram and philosophy",
          "type": "facts",
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Trigram",
              "value": "☰ · Keon · 건 (乾 / 天)"
            },
            {
              "label": "Element",
              "value": "Heaven and Light (Genesis & Creative Origin)"
            },
            {
              "label": "Core concept",
              "value": "Keon is the creative force which inhabits all physical forms. Keon is powerful and aggressive, and it is represented by heaven and light."
            },
            {
              "label": "Belt level",
              "value": "White Belt (10th – 9th Geup)"
            },
            {
              "label": "Dialectic",
              "value": "Pure creative force; opposite Gon (Earth). In Gon is realized the nature of Keon; and in Keon, the nature of Gon."
            },
            {
              "label": "Direction sequence",
              "value": "9:00 -> 3:00 -> 12:00 -> 3:00 -> 9:00 -> 12:00 -> 9:00 -> 3:00 -> 6:00"
            },
            {
              "label": "Kihap on step",
              "value": "16"
            },
            {
              "label": "Target duration",
              "value": "30–35 sec"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "directive",
          "title": "Philosophical directive",
          "type": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "The actions in Taegeuk 1 are associated with Keon. Direction of movement follows the trigram that represents Keon, embodying the genesis of creation, upright grandeur, and powerful forward conviction."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "introduced",
          "title": "Key techniques introduced",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Ready stance (Gibon Joon-bi Seogi)",
            "Basic walking stance (Ap-seogi, 50/50 balance)",
            "Forward stance (Ap-kubi, 70/30 weight)",
            "Two front snap kicks (Ap-chagi)",
            "Low downward block (Arae-makki)",
            "High face block (Olgul-makki)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "floor-plan",
          "title": "Floor plan lines",
          "type": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Line 1 (Top / Heaven / 9:00 ↔ 3:00)",
              "subtitle": "Heaven & Pure Light",
              "body": "Advances forward with front kick and reverse punch on both flanks, generating the top solid Yang line (—–).",
              "bullets": [],
              "facts": [
                {
                  "label": "Steps",
                  "value": "Steps 11–14"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Line",
                  "value": "Yang (solid)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Line 2 (Middle / Man / 3:00 ↔ 9:00)",
              "subtitle": "Man & Harmonious Action",
              "body": "Low block and direct punch along the center 12:00 axis, followed by advancing inside blocks and reverse punches, forming the middle solid Yang line (—–).",
              "bullets": [],
              "facts": [
                {
                  "label": "Steps",
                  "value": "Steps 5–10"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Line",
                  "value": "Yang (solid)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Line 3 (Bottom / Earth / 9:00 ↔ 3:00)",
              "subtitle": "Earth & Grounded Beginning",
              "body": "Low downward blocks advance with reverse middle punches on both sides, creating the foundational bottom solid Yang line (—–).",
              "bullets": [],
              "facts": [
                {
                  "label": "Steps",
                  "value": "Steps 1–4"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Line",
                  "value": "Yang (solid)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "principles",
          "title": "Execution principles",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Technique (기술): Downward blocks must snap exactly two fists above the front thigh; punches must target the solar plexus centerline.",
            "Knowledge (지식): The pattern traces the Chinese character 王 (King), where three advancing steps establish the three solid lines of the Keon trigram.",
            "Attitude (태도): Perform with upright grandeur and clear cadence, embodying the genesis of creation and the morning sun.",
            "Eye Focus (시선): Pivot head and eyes toward the imaginary opponent at 9:00, 3:00, 12:00, and 6:00 before initiating footwork.",
            "Posture & Balance (중심): Maintain 50/50 balance in walking stances (Ap-seogi) with 1 foot-length spacing, transitioning to rooted 70/30 weight in forward stances (Ap-kubi).",
            "Timing & Rhythm (완급): Complete each technique cleanly with a momentary focal pause before transitioning smoothly without hesitation.",
            "Power (힘): Stay relaxed during chambering from the opposite shoulder or hip; deliver explosive muscular lock at impact.",
            "Breathing & Kihop (기합): Inhale during preparation; exhale sharply through the Danjeon on impact, releasing a thunderous Kihap on the final punch."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "major-deductions",
          "title": "Major deductions (−0.3)",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Loss of balance or staggering upon landing front kicks (-0.3).",
            "Incorrect movement or missing step (-0.3).",
            "Omitting the final Kihap or delivering it prematurely (-0.3).",
            "Facing the wrong clock coordinate (-0.3)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "minor-deductions",
          "title": "Minor deductions (−0.1)",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Blocking fist dropping below knee level or wrist bent during Arae-makki (-0.1).",
            "Punching off the solar plexus centerline (-0.1).",
            "Rear heel lifting off the mat during forward stances (Ap-kubi) (-0.1).",
            "High block resting against the forehead without 1-fist clearance (-0.1)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "steps",
          "title": "Movement sequence",
          "type": "steps",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Pivot on the right foot turning left 90° into Left Ap-seogi (Walking Stance). Execute Left Arae-makki (Low Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Advance forward into Right Ap-seogi. Execute Right Momtong Bandae-jireugi (Reverse Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] Turn clockwise 180° into Right Ap-seogi. Execute Right Arae-makki (Low Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] Advance forward into Left Ap-seogi. Execute Left Momtong Bandae-jireugi (Reverse Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[12 o’clock] Turn counterclockwise 90° into Left Ap-kubi (Forward Stance). Execute Left Arae-makki (Low Block). In the same stance, execute Right Momtong Baro-jireugi (Direct Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] With the left foot fixed, move right foot to left heel and turn right into Right Ap-seogi. Execute Left Momtong An-makki (Inside Middle Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] Advance forward into Left Ap-seogi. Execute Right Momtong Baro-jireugi (Direct Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Pivot on the ball of the right foot, turn counterclockwise 180° into Left Ap-seogi. Execute Right Momtong An-makki (Inside Middle Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Advance forward into Right Ap-seogi. Execute Left Momtong Baro-jireugi (Direct Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[12 o’clock] Turn right 90° into Right Ap-kubi (Forward Stance). Execute Right Arae-makki (Low Block). In the same stance, execute Left Momtong Baro-jireugi (Direct Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Bring left foot to right heel, turn left 90° into Left Ap-seogi. Execute Left Olgul-makki (High Face Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[9 o’clock] Execute Right Ap-chagi (Front Snap Kick), land forward into Right Ap-seogi with Right Momtong Bandae-jireugi (Reverse Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] Turn clockwise 180° into Right Ap-seogi. Execute Right Olgul-makki (High Face Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[3 o’clock] Execute Left Ap-chagi (Front Snap Kick), land forward into Left Ap-seogi with Left Momtong Bandae-jireugi (Reverse Middle Punch).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[6 o’clock] Pivoting on the right foot, turn clockwise 90° toward the rear into Left Ap-kubi (Forward Stance). Execute Left Arae-makki (Low Block).",
              "details": []
            },
            {
              "title": "",
              "body": "[6 o’clock] Advance forward into Right Ap-kubi (Forward Stance). Execute Right Momtong Bandae-jireugi (Reverse Middle Punch) with explosive Kihap! On Ba-ro, pivot on right foot, turn body left back to Gibon Joon-bi Seogi.",
              "details": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "key-details",
          "title": "Key details",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Maintain 50/50 balance in walking stance (Ap-seogi) with exactly 1 foot-length spacing and 30° rear foot angle.",
            "Chamber the low block fist at the opposite shoulder before snapping down 2 fists above thigh.",
            "Punch directly along the center solar-plexus axis of your body with simultaneous hip twist.",
            "Breathe out smoothly through the Danjeon on each final block and strike impact."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "mistakes",
          "title": "Common mistakes",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Dropping the blocking fist below knee level or flexing the wrist during Arae-makki (-0.1).",
            "Over-stepping the forward stance, causing the rear heel to lift off the floor (-0.1).",
            "Rushing the 180° turns without cleanly pivoting on the ball of the foot (-0.1)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tips",
          "title": "Coaching tips",
          "type": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            "Stance Simplicity: This form is composed almost entirely of walking stances (Ap-seogi), punctuated by long forward stances (Ap-kubi) only along the center axis.",
            "Step 6 to 7 Transition: Pull your right foot forward only about half a step (not a full step), then pivot cleanly 90° to the right on the ball of the rear foot.",
            "Step 10 to 11 Chamber: At the completion of step 10, instead of chambering the punching hand, chamber the belt hand at the opposite shoulder to prepare for the low block.",
            "Step 15 to 16 Pivot: When turning 90° toward the rear line, do not move the right foot—pivot on the ball of your right foot while swinging your left leg around, and chamber your left hand."
          ]
        },
